Dragon Blast (2026-11-13): XenosRecomp on Raging Blast 2's shaders (13 of its 538 vertex shaders did not compile).

- A constant named like a swizzle ("z" in RB2's engine shaders) became "#define z g_C(n)" and broke every ".z":
  such names (only x/y/z/w or r/g/b/a letters) get the prefix "c_".
- Vertex shaders reading PSIZE (point sprites) had an input without [[vk::location]] (DXC: "partial explicit stage
  input location assignment"): PointSize 0 is location 23 in the table the Renut's vertex layouts share (its enum
  gets the name PointSize next to PSize). An input still missing from the table is reported instead of the assert,
  which a Release build drops.

